	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9953"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146" title="View the profile of simplee">simplee</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 127<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/devil1.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								smoked again................    ranger down!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9953#msg9953"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9953#msg9953">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #39 on:</b> August 11, 2004, 07:52:44 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9940#msg9940">Quote from: silverblades on August 10, 2004, 08:24:58 pm</a></div><div class="quote">as far as your pulling it stinks pulling 5 6 or 7 mobs and expecting the ranger to root them all is idiotic to begin with and if you cant handle pulling 2 or 3 mobs at a time then perhaps its time for you to start another toon that doesnt have to pull.       silverblades.<br /></div><br />At no point was there a 5, 6 or 7 mob pull from what the screenshots show.  There was one 3 pull, which seems not to be disputed by any members of the group.  So apparently he can handle pulling 2-3 mobs at a time, and seemingly was only pulling 1 or 2 most of the time unless his lull was resisted.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9941#msg9941">Quote from: silverblades on August 10, 2004, 09:16:04 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Another thing id like to say id i was parking adds as they came they just kept resisisting and breaking my roots so for those people who werent there need to keep their posts to themselves miss simplee mee. who are u to talk about the situation when you werent even present for it.<br /></div><br />Resists and breaks happen.  Try kiting.  Try using snare, or flame lick... both are sure-fire aggro getters.  Use the taunt key if you need to.  As for keeping posts to myself... this is a public board, where all people are free to express their opinion.  You are, I am, as is anyone else.  We may not know the full story, but seeing as the screenshots are continuous, we&#039;ve got a pretty good idea as to what happened.<br /><br />I&#039;m still baffled as to why you decided to call me out on this.  I&#039;m certainly not the only one who mentioned your &quot;abilities&quot;, nor was my assessment the harshest.  I&#039;m a ranger.  I have my own ideas as to how the class should be played, and from what I&#039;m reading, I don&#039;t think my ideas are that far off base.&nbsp; I don&#039;t claim to be the best ranger... not even close, but I do think I have a pretty good idea as to how to play the class to maximize all the tools we are given.&nbsp; Those include, but are not limited to, CC, healing, and tanking.<br /><br />Oh, and do me a favor... no more tells.  If you want to discuss this, do it in PM&#039;s (although I&#039;d appreciate some form of punctuation if you decide to pursue this route). I don&#039;t appreciate tells regarding posts I made a week ago, especially when you tell me that I shouldn&#039;t post unless I can stand to discuss it in game.  When I&#039;m in game, I&#039;m having fun, and usually pretty busy.  If you didn&#039;t get a response fast enough last night it was probably because I was in 5 channels, on a raid, and in tell hell.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: August 11, 2004, 07:57:13 am by simplee</i> &#187;
